A||N||6||jaguiler||Legal Question for Everyone!! Abandoned Car!!!||||6||
Z||000000||jaguiler||08-14-2001||07:29 PM||||Hello,<P>Near where I work there is an abandoned car in a parking garage!!  Requires some fix up work...  The car is in Maryland, Baltimore City to be exact.  Does anyone know what I have to do to take this car and claim it as my own? Legally, I mean.<P><P>------------------<BR><BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||08-14-2001||08:00 PM||||I had the same question once.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001760.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001760.html</A> <P>It was a pretty nice 84.  Sat there for 3 years.  Finally found the owner, but wouldn't come down to a reasonable price.  One day recently it disappeared, no idea what happened to it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||operator64||08-14-2001||08:01 PM||||   From state to state and town to town the laws will differ, but one of the biggest things to have on your side is owning the property wher any vehicle is abandoned at. Thereafter get with the local police or Sherrifs department on the proper way of taking possesion of it.<BR>                   Operator<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||08-14-2001||08:14 PM||||In some states if you don't know the owner, you can get a bonded title.  You have to get an estimate for the current value(lets say $300).  That way if you put money into the car making it worth more (lets say $2000), and the original owner shows up and wants the car, all he gets is the $300 for value of the car when you got it.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||08-14-2001||09:23 PM||||Our laws in Australia are good on abandoned vehicles. If a car sits for more than 6 months on the roadside while unregistered it is fair game. Well unless the owner lives right where the car is parked. I found a $10,000 Mercededs once abandoned, didn't take it but looked into. Sure enough the day I went to take it, it had been claimed, legally. For Free. I was very dirty with myself for not getting up early that morning.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000005||fierohoho||08-14-2001||10:05 PM||||jaguiler, two ideas.<P>Check with your Dept of Motor Vehicles, you may be able to have them run the license plate or VIN for a small fee, if they can you could then contact the registered owner and see if he would sell it.<P>Or, contact the city where the parking garage is located and find out who the property owner is and contact him/her and see what they have to say about the car.<P>I would guess the owner or friend of the owner/manager is letting someone store the car there. <P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||08-14-2001||10:54 PM||||Isnt registered to Chandra Levy is it? Does it have a body lying in it?||||reg||1
